IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sawhs-dates`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2012 (SA) -- the rules a worker meets when hurt, put at risk or treated badly at work, or
-- when bringing or pressing a claim about it: who is a worker (ss 5, 7); the primary duty owed to the worker (s 19); the
-- worker's own duty to follow instructions (s 28(c)); the offences and penalties for breach of a duty, industrial
-- manslaughter included (Part 2 Division 5, ss 4(2)-(4), 30-34); incident notification (Part 3, ss 35-39, with regs 699
-- and 699A of the Work Health and Safety Regulations 2012); the right to cease unsafe work (Part 5 Division 6, ss 83-88,
-- with reg 24; s 103); work health and safety disputes in SAET (Part 5 Division 7A, ss 102A, 102B, 102F, and s 260A);
-- discriminatory, coercive and misleading conduct and the civil and criminal remedies for it (Part 6, ss 104-115);
-- compensation for an inspector's entry powers (s 184); review of decisions (Part 12, ss 223, 224, 226, 228, 229); the
-- request for a prosecution and the prosecution time limits (ss 230-232); civil liability (s 267); no contracting out
-- and no levies on workers (ss 272, 273).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in sawhs-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "if", "only if",
-- "unless", "cannot", "does not", "must not", "may only", "while", a period the Act fixes); or NOTHING where the Act does
-- not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Judgments the Act leaves to others ("reasonable
-- concern", "reasonably considers", "reasonable excuse", "merits criminal punishment", "unjustifiable", "unreasonably
-- failed", "just", "frivolous", what a court or SAET finds proved) are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a
-- guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of South
-- Australia, CC BY 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Work Health and Safety Act 2012 (SA)`

§§ `ss 5, 7 -- who is a worker`

-- s 7(1): "A person is a worker if the person carries out work in any capacity for a person conducting a business or
-- undertaking, including work as -- (a) an employee; ... (h) a volunteer; or (i) a person of a prescribed class."
-- s 7(2): a police officer is a worker. s 7(3): "The person conducting the business or undertaking is also a worker if
-- the person is an individual who carries out work in that business or undertaking." s 5(1)(b): conducted "whether or
-- not ... for profit or gain"; s 5(7): "A volunteer association does not conduct a business or undertaking"; s 5(8): a
-- group of volunteers working together for community purposes where none of them employs anyone to carry out work for
-- it. No regulation prescribes a class under s 7(1)(i) (the Regulations, deposited, were searched). An "if"
-- definition: JUST FALSE when no limb holds.
GIVEN `I carry out work for a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a volunteer association that employs no one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I conduct the business myself and work in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7 -- I am a worker` `I carry out work for a business or undertaking` `it is a volunteer association that employs no one` `I am a police officer` `I conduct the business myself and work in it` MEANS
    IF `I am a police officer`
       OR `I conduct the business myself and work in it`
       OR (`I carry out work for a business or undertaking` AND (NOT `it is a volunteer association that employs no one`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 19 -- the primary duty of care owed to me`

-- s 19(1): the person conducting a business or undertaking "must ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, the health
-- and safety of -- (a) workers engaged, or caused to be engaged by the person; and (b) workers whose activities in
-- carrying out work are influenced or directed by the person, while the workers are at work in the business or
-- undertaking." (2): "... that the health and safety of other persons is not put at risk from work carried out as part
-- of the conduct of the business or undertaking." Whether the duty was met (s 18) is a judgment and not asked here. The
-- "while" of (1) fails: JUST FALSE unless (2) reaches the person; neither limb: NOTHING-kind: a duty limited in its own
-- wording, and the case falls outside it (fork F4).
GIVEN `the business engaged me or caused me to be engaged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business influences or directs my work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was at work in the business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `work of the business could put my health and safety at risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 -- the business owes me the primary duty of care` `the business engaged me or caused me to be engaged` `the business influences or directs my work` `I was at work in the business` `work of the business could put my health and safety at risk` MEANS
    IF ((`the business engaged me or caused me to be engaged` OR `the business influences or directs my work`) AND `I was at work in the business`)
       OR `work of the business could put my health and safety at risk`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the business engaged me or caused me to be engaged` OR `the business influences or directs my work`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 28(c) -- my duty to follow instructions`

-- s 28: "While at work, a worker must -- ... (c) comply, so far as the worker is reasonably able, with any reasonable
-- instruction that is given by the person conducting the business or undertaking to allow the person to comply with this
-- Act". Not at work: JUST FALSE (the "while"). An instruction that is not reasonable, not given to allow compliance with
-- the Act, or beyond what the worker is reasonably able to do: NOTHING-kind: a duty limited in its own wording (fork F5).
GIVEN `I am at work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business gave the instruction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instruction is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was given to allow the business to comply with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am reasonably able to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(c) -- I must comply with the instruction` `I am at work` `the business gave the instruction` `the instruction is reasonable` `it was given to allow the business to comply with the Act` `I am reasonably able to comply` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am at work`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the business gave the instruction` AND `the instruction is reasonable` AND `it was given to allow the business to comply with the Act` AND `I am reasonably able to comply`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part 2 Division 5 -- offences against the duty owed to me`

-- Who the duty holder is, for the offences and their penalties: "an individual (other than as a person conducting a
-- business or undertaking or as an officer ...)", "an individual as a person conducting a business or undertaking or as
-- an officer ...", "a body corporate" (ss 30A, 31-33); s 34(3): "An unincorporated association does not commit an offence
-- under this Act ... for a failure to comply with a duty or obligation imposed on the unincorporated association".
DECLARE `Duty holder` IS ONE OF
    `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it`
    `a body corporate conducting the business or undertaking`
    `another individual, such as a worker or other person at the workplace`
    `an unincorporated association`

DECLARE `Offence made out` IS ONE OF
    `industrial manslaughter (s 30A)`
    `a Category 1 offence (s 31)`
    `a Category 2 offence (s 32)`
    `a Category 3 offence (s 33)`
    `no offence under Part 2 on these facts`

-- The facts of one case: what the duty holder did to the individual (the worker, or the family member who died).
DECLARE `Duty case` HAS
    `the holder`                          IS A `Duty holder`
    `the holder is a volunteer`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the duty is a duty under s 28 or 29` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a duty was owed`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the duty was not complied with`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it exposed the individual to a risk of death or serious injury or illness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder had no reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct fell so greatly short of the standard of care of a reasonable person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct carried so high a risk of death or serious injury or illness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct merits criminal punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder was aware of a substantial risk of death or serious injury or illness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `taking the risk was unjustifiable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual died`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct substantially contributed to the death` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 34(2): "A volunteer does not commit an offence under this Division for a failure to comply with a health and safety
-- duty, except a duty under section 28 or 29." (s 30A is in this Division.) s 34(3): unincorporated associations.
-- s 34(1) (a volunteer officer of a strata or community titles corporation and the s 27 duty) is within s 34(2).
GIVEN c IS A `Duty case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 34 -- the holder is exempt` c IF
    (c's `the holder` EQUALS `an unincorporated association`)
    OR (c's `the holder is a volunteer` AND (NOT c's `the duty is a duty under s 28 or 29`))

-- s 4(2): "a person engages in conduct with gross negligence if the conduct involves -- (a) such a great falling short of
-- the standard of care that a reasonable person would exercise in the circumstances; and (b) such a high risk of causing
-- the death or serious injury or illness of an individual, that the conduct merits criminal punishment for the offence."
GIVEN c IS A `Duty case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(2) -- the conduct was grossly negligent` c IF
    c's `the conduct fell so greatly short of the standard of care of a reasonable person`
    AND c's `the conduct carried so high a risk of death or serious injury or illness`
    AND c's `the conduct merits criminal punishment`

-- s 4(3): "a person is reckless as to the risk to an individual of death or serious injury or illness if -- (a) the
-- person is aware of a substantial risk that death or serious injury or illness will happen; and (b) having regard to the
-- circumstances known to the person, it is unjustifiable to take the risk." (4): unjustifiability "is a question of fact".
GIVEN c IS A `Duty case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(3) -- the holder was reckless` c IF
    c's `the holder was aware of a substantial risk of death or serious injury or illness`
    AND c's `taking the risk was unjustifiable`

-- s 30A(1): "A person (being a person conducting a business or undertaking or an officer of a person conducting a business
-- or undertaking) commits an industrial manslaughter offence if -- (a) the person has a health and safety duty; and (b)
-- the person engages in conduct that breaches that duty; and (c) the conduct causes the death of an individual to whom
-- that duty is owed; and (d) the person -- (i) engages in the conduct with gross negligence; or (ii) is reckless as to the
-- risk to an individual of death or serious injury or illness." (2): "conduct causes the death of an individual if it
-- substantially contributes to the death."
GIVEN c IS A `Duty case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30A -- industrial manslaughter is made out` c IF
    (NOT (c's `the holder` EQUALS `another individual, such as a worker or other person at the workplace`))
    AND (NOT (c's `the holder` EQUALS `an unincorporated association`))
    AND c's `a duty was owed`
    AND c's `the duty was not complied with`
    AND c's `the individual died`
    AND c's `the conduct substantially contributed to the death`
    AND (`s 4(2) -- the conduct was grossly negligent` c OR `s 4(3) -- the holder was reckless` c)

-- s 31(1): a health and safety duty; "without reasonable excuse, engages in conduct that exposes an individual to whom
-- that duty is owed to a risk of death or serious injury or illness"; and gross negligence or recklessness. s 32: the
-- duty, a failure to comply, and the failure "exposes an individual to a risk of death or serious injury or illness".
-- s 33: the duty and a failure to comply. The most serious offence the facts make out is answered (s 30A(3) lets the
-- trier of fact who acquits of industrial manslaughter convict of a Category 1, 2 or 3 offence). Whether a court would find
-- each fact is for the court: the facts are inputs (fork F12).
GIVEN c IS A `Duty case`
GIVETH A `Offence made out`
`the most serious offence made out` c MEANS
    IF `s 34 -- the holder is exempt` c
    THEN `no offence under Part 2 on these facts`
    ELSE IF `s 30A -- industrial manslaughter is made out` c
         THEN `industrial manslaughter (s 30A)`
         ELSE IF c's `a duty was owed` AND c's `it exposed the individual to a risk of death or serious injury or illness` AND c's `the holder had no reasonable excuse` AND (`s 4(2) -- the conduct was grossly negligent` c OR `s 4(3) -- the holder was reckless` c)
              THEN `a Category 1 offence (s 31)`
              ELSE IF c's `a duty was owed` AND c's `the duty was not complied with` AND c's `it exposed the individual to a risk of death or serious injury or illness`
                   THEN `a Category 2 offence (s 32)`
                   ELSE IF c's `a duty was owed` AND c's `the duty was not complied with`
                        THEN `a Category 3 offence (s 33)`
                        ELSE `no offence under Part 2 on these facts`

-- The maximum fine, in dollars, for the offence and the kind of holder (ss 30A, 31, 32, 33, "Maximum penalty"). NOTHING
-- where the Act sets no fine: industrial manslaughter by an individual (imprisonment only), and a holder who cannot commit
-- the offence (NOTHING-kind: the text is silent).
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence made out`, h IS A `Duty holder`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the maximum fine for` o `by` h MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `an unincorporated association` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it` THEN
        CONSIDER o
        WHEN `industrial manslaughter (s 30A)` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `a Category 1 offence (s 31)` THEN JUST 600000
        WHEN `a Category 2 offence (s 32)` THEN JUST 300000
        WHEN `a Category 3 offence (s 33)` THEN JUST 100000
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `a body corporate conducting the business or undertaking` THEN
        CONSIDER o
        WHEN `industrial manslaughter (s 30A)` THEN JUST 18000000
        WHEN `a Category 1 offence (s 31)` THEN JUST 3000000
        WHEN `a Category 2 offence (s 32)` THEN JUST 1500000
        WHEN `a Category 3 offence (s 33)` THEN JUST 500000
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER o
        WHEN `a Category 1 offence (s 31)` THEN JUST 300000
        WHEN `a Category 2 offence (s 32)` THEN JUST 150000
        WHEN `a Category 3 offence (s 33)` THEN JUST 50000
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The maximum term of imprisonment, in years. Only industrial manslaughter (20 years) and a Category 1 offence (5 years)
-- carry imprisonment, and only for an individual; NOTHING otherwise (NOTHING-kind: the text sets none).
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence made out`, h IS A `Duty holder`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the maximum years of imprisonment for` o `by` h MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it` THEN
        CONSIDER o
        WHEN `industrial manslaughter (s 30A)` THEN JUST 20
        WHEN `a Category 1 offence (s 31)` THEN JUST 5
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `another individual, such as a worker or other person at the workplace` THEN
        CONSIDER o
        WHEN `a Category 1 offence (s 31)` THEN JUST 5
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Part 3 -- notifiable incidents`

-- s 36: "serious injury or illness of a person means an injury or illness requiring the person to have -- (a) immediate
-- treatment as an in-patient in a hospital; or (b) immediate treatment for -- (i) the amputation of any part of his or
-- her body; (ii) a serious head injury; (iii) a serious eye injury; (iv) a serious burn; (v) the separation of his or her
-- skin from an underlying tissue (such as degloving or scalping); (vi) a spinal injury; (vii) the loss of a bodily
-- function; (viii) serious lacerations; or (c) medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance, and includes
-- any other injury or illness prescribed by the regulations but does not include an illness or injury of a prescribed
-- kind." Reg 699: "each of the following conditions is a serious illness: (a) any infection to which the carrying out of
-- work is a significant contributing factor ...; (b) the following occupational zoonoses contracted in the course of work
-- involving handling or contact with animals ...: Q fever; Anthrax; Leptospirosis; Brucellosis; Hendra Virus; Avian
-- Influenza; Psittacosis." No regulation prescribes a kind excluded.
DECLARE `Treatment required` IS ONE OF
    `immediate treatment as an in-patient in a hospital`
    `immediate treatment for the amputation of part of the body`
    `immediate treatment for a serious head injury`
    `immediate treatment for a serious eye injury`
    `immediate treatment for a serious burn`
    `immediate treatment for degloving or scalping`
    `immediate treatment for a spinal injury`
    `immediate treatment for the loss of a bodily function`
    `immediate treatment for serious lacerations`
    `medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance`
    `an infection to which carrying out work was a significant contributing factor (reg 699(a))`
    `a listed zoonosis contracted in work with animals or animal products (reg 699(b))`
    `other treatment, or none`
    `no injury or illness`

-- A listed head (the Act's or reg 699's): JUST TRUE. Anything else: JUST FALSE (a "means" definition, with the
-- regulations it hands to deposited and searched).
GIVEN t IS A `Treatment required`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36 -- it is a serious injury or illness` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `other treatment, or none` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `no injury or illness` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 37: "dangerous incident means an incident in relation to a workplace that exposes a worker or any other person to a
-- serious risk to a person's health or safety emanating from an immediate or imminent exposure to -- (a) ... (k) ...; or
-- (l) any other event prescribed by the regulations, but does not include an incident of a prescribed kind." Reg 699A:
-- "the unplanned loss of control of heavy earthmoving machinery (including failure of braking or steering) at a mine is a
-- dangerous incident" -- read as an event under (l), so the serious-risk words of s 37 still apply (fork F6).
DECLARE `Exposure` IS ONE OF
    `an uncontrolled escape, spillage or leakage of a substance`
    `an uncontrolled implosion, explosion or fire`
    `an uncontrolled escape of gas or steam`
    `an uncontrolled escape of a pressurised substance`
    `electric shock`
    `the fall or release from a height of any plant, substance or thing`
    `the collapse, overturning, failure or malfunction of, or damage to, plant that must be authorised`
    `the collapse or partial collapse of a structure`
    `the collapse or failure of an excavation or its shoring`
    `the inrush of water, mud or gas in workings, an underground excavation or tunnel`
    `the interruption of the main ventilation in an underground excavation or tunnel`
    `the unplanned loss of control of heavy earthmoving machinery at a mine (reg 699A)`
    `another kind of event`
    `no exposure`

-- The "means" definition: JUST FALSE where it is not an incident in relation to a workplace, there was no serious risk,
-- the exposure was not immediate or imminent, or the event is not listed (the regulations deposited and searched); a
-- listed exposure: JUST TRUE.
GIVEN `it was an incident in relation to a workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone was exposed to a serious risk to health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exposure was immediate or imminent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exposure` IS AN `Exposure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37 -- it is a dangerous incident` `it was an incident in relation to a workplace` `someone was exposed to a serious risk to health or safety` `the exposure was immediate or imminent` `the exposure` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it was an incident in relation to a workplace`)
       OR (NOT `someone was exposed to a serious risk to health or safety`)
       OR (NOT `the exposure was immediate or imminent`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the exposure`
         WHEN `another kind of event` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `no exposure` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 35: "notifiable incident means -- (a) the death of a person; or (b) a serious injury or illness of a person; or
-- (c) a dangerous incident." A closed "means" list.
GIVEN `a person died` IS A BOOLEAN, `serious` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `dangerous` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35 -- it is a notifiable incident` `a person died` `serious` `dangerous` MEANS
    IF `a person died` OR (`serious` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`dangerous` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`serious` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`dangerous` EQUALS NOTHING)
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 38(1): the person who conducts a business or undertaking "must ensure that the regulator is notified immediately
-- after becoming aware that a notifiable incident arising out of the conduct of the business or undertaking has
-- occurred." Not notifiable, or not arising out of this business: JUST FALSE for this business (fork F7).
GIVEN `notifiable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `it arose out of the conduct of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(1) -- the business must notify the regulator` `notifiable` `it arose out of the conduct of the business` MEANS
    IF NOT `it arose out of the conduct of the business`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `notifiable`

-- s 38(7): "must keep a record of each notifiable incident for at least 5 years from the day that notice of the incident
-- is given to the regulator". "From the day" excludes the day: the last day is the fifth anniversary (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 38(7) -- the last day the record must be kept` `the day notice was given` MEANS
    `the anniversary` 5 `years after` `the day notice was given`

-- s 39(1): the person with management or control of the workplace "must ensure so far as is reasonably practicable, that
-- the site where the incident occurred is not disturbed until an inspector arrives at the site or any earlier time that
-- an inspector directs." (3): "Subsection (1) does not prevent any action -- (a) to assist an injured person; or (b) to
-- remove a deceased person; or (c) that is essential to make the site safe or to minimise the risk of a further
-- notifiable incident; or (d) that is associated with a police investigation; or (e) for which an inspector or the
-- regulator has given permission."
DECLARE `Purpose of the action` IS ONE OF
    `to assist an injured person`
    `to remove a deceased person`
    `to make the site safe or minimise the risk of a further notifiable incident`
    `associated with a police investigation`
    `permitted by an inspector or the regulator`
    `another purpose`

-- JUST TRUE: s 39(1) forbids the action. JUST FALSE: the inspector has arrived or the directed time has come ("until"),
-- or s 39(3) applies ("does not prevent"). Not a notifiable incident: NOTHING-kind: outside the section's scope.
-- "So far as is reasonably practicable" is not asked (fork F13).
GIVEN `notifiable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an inspector has arrived or the directed time has come` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose` IS A `Purpose of the action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39 -- the site must not be disturbed by the action` `notifiable` `an inspector has arrived or the directed time has come` `the purpose` MEANS
    IF NOT (`notifiable` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `an inspector has arrived or the directed time has come`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the purpose`
              WHEN `another purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 5 Division 6 -- the right to cease unsafe work`

-- s 84: "A worker may cease, or refuse to carry out, work if the worker has a reasonable concern that to carry out the
-- work would expose the worker to a serious risk to the worker's health or safety, emanating from an immediate or
-- imminent exposure to a hazard." s 85A: the availability of a SAET dispute under Division 7A is not relevant to whether
-- the concern is reasonable. s 103: "Nothing in this Part applies to a worker who is a prisoner in custody in a prison or
-- police gaol." An "if", and a flat negative: JUST FALSE when either fails.
GIVEN `I am a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a prisoner in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have a reasonable concern` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work would expose me to a serious risk to my health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk comes from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84 -- I may cease or refuse the work` `I am a worker` `I am a prisoner in custody` `I have a reasonable concern` `the work would expose me to a serious risk to my health or safety` `the risk comes from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard` MEANS
    IF `I am a worker` AND (NOT `I am a prisoner in custody`) AND `I have a reasonable concern` AND `the work would expose me to a serious risk to my health or safety` AND `the risk comes from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 85(1): a health and safety representative "may direct a worker who is in a work group represented by the
-- representative to cease work if the representative has a reasonable concern" of the same risk. (2): "must not give a
-- worker a direction to cease work unless the matter is not resolved after -- (a) consulting ...; and (b) attempting to
-- resolve the matter as an issue under Division 5". (3): without that, "if the risk is so serious and immediate or
-- imminent that it is not reasonable to consult before giving the direction". (6): "cannot give a direction ... unless the
-- representative has" completed the prescribed initial training, or done it before for another work group, or equivalent
-- training under a corresponding WHS law. s 103: not for a worker who is a prisoner in custody.
GIVEN `I am in the representative's work group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a prisoner in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representative has a reasonable concern of a serious risk from an immediate or imminent hazard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representative has the required training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representative consulted the business and tried issue resolution, and it was not resolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk was so serious and immediate that it was not reasonable to consult first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85 -- the representative could direct me to cease work` `I am in the representative's work group` `I am a prisoner in custody` `the representative has a reasonable concern of a serious risk from an immediate or imminent hazard` `the representative has the required training` `the representative consulted the business and tried issue resolution, and it was not resolved` `the risk was so serious and immediate that it was not reasonable to consult first` MEANS
    IF `I am in the representative's work group`
       AND (NOT `I am a prisoner in custody`)
       AND `the representative has a reasonable concern of a serious risk from an immediate or imminent hazard`
       AND `the representative has the required training`
       AND (`the representative consulted the business and tried issue resolution, and it was not resolved` OR `the risk was so serious and immediate that it was not reasonable to consult first`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `How I ceased work` IS ONE OF
    `I ceased or refused the work myself (s 84)`
    `on a direction of a health and safety representative (s 85)`

-- s 83: "cease work under this Division means -- (a) to cease, or refuse, to carry out work under section 84; or (b) to
-- cease work on a direction under section 85."
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I ceased work`, `s 84 answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `s 85 answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83 -- I ceased work under the Division` `how` `s 84 answer` `s 85 answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `I ceased or refused the work myself (s 84)` THEN `s 84 answer`
    OTHERWISE `s 85 answer`

-- s 86: "A worker who ceases work under this Division (otherwise than under a direction from a health and safety
-- representative) must -- (a) as soon as practicable, notify the person conducting the business or undertaking that the
-- worker has ceased work under this Division unless the worker ceased work under a direction from a health and safety
-- representative; and (b) remain available to carry out suitable alternative work." Ceased on a representative's
-- direction: JUST FALSE (the "otherwise than" and the "unless" both say so). Not under the Division: NOTHING-kind: the
-- section's duty does not arise (fork F7).
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I ceased work`, `under the Division` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(a) -- I must notify the business that I ceased work` `how` `under the Division` MEANS
    IF NOT (`under the Division` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `how`
         WHEN `on a direction of a health and safety representative (s 85)` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 88: "If a worker ceases work under this Division, that action does not affect the continuity of engagement of the
-- worker for prescribed purposes if the worker has not unreasonably failed to comply with a direction to carry out
-- suitable alternative work -- (a) at the same or another workplace; and (b) that was safe and appropriate for the worker
-- to carry out." Reg 24: the prescribed purposes "are the assessment of eligibility for, or the calculation of benefits
-- for, any benefit or entitlement associated with the worker's engagement, including ... (a) remuneration and promotion,
-- as affected by seniority; (b) superannuation benefits; (c) leave entitlements; (d) any entitlement to notice of
-- termination of the engagement." JUST TRUE: protected. JUST FALSE: the worker unreasonably failed to follow a direction
-- to safe and appropriate alternative work (the "if" fails). Not under the Division: NOTHING-kind: outside the section.
GIVEN `under the Division` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `I was directed to safe and appropriate suitable alternative work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I unreasonably failed to comply with that direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88 -- my continuity of engagement is not affected` `under the Division` `I was directed to safe and appropriate suitable alternative work` `I unreasonably failed to comply with that direction` MEANS
    IF NOT (`under the Division` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `I was directed to safe and appropriate suitable alternative work` AND `I unreasonably failed to comply with that direction`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 5 Division 7A -- work health and safety disputes in SAET`

-- s 102A: "dispute means a dispute about a WHS matter that exists between any of the following persons: (a) a person
-- conducting a business or undertaking; (b) a worker affected by the WHS matter (or the personal representative of a
-- deceased worker who was affected by the WHS matter); (c) a health and safety representative affected by the WHS matter;
-- (d) a relevant union for the WHS matter"; "WHS matter means any of the following matters: (a) access to information by
-- a health and safety representative under section 70(1)(c); (b) a request by a health and safety representative for an
-- assistant to have access to the workplace under section 70(1)(g); (c) a matter about work health and safety that is an
-- issue to which Division 5 applies; (d) an issue about cessation of work under Division 6."
DECLARE `My part in the dispute` IS ONE OF
    `a worker affected by the matter`
    `the personal representative of a deceased worker who was affected`
    `a health and safety representative affected by the matter`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `WHS matter` IS ONE OF
    `a work health and safety issue to which Division 5 applies`
    `an issue about cessation of work under Division 6`
    `a representative's access to information or an assistant's access (s 70(1)(c), (g))`
    `something else`

-- s 102B(1): "This section applies if a dispute remains unresolved at least 24 hours after any of the parties to the
-- dispute has, under another provision of this Part, asked the regulator to appoint an inspector to assist in resolving
-- the dispute." (2): "A party to the dispute may give SAET written notice of the dispute." s 103: not for a worker who is
-- a prisoner in custody. "Means" definitions and an "applies if": JUST FALSE when any part fails.
GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part in the dispute`
      `the matter` IS A `WHS matter`
      `I am a prisoner in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party asked the regulator to appoint an inspector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dispute is still unresolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours since that request` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102B -- I may give SAET notice of the dispute` `my part` `the matter` `I am a prisoner in custody` `a party asked the regulator to appoint an inspector` `the dispute is still unresolved` `the hours since that request` MEANS
    IF (`my part` EQUALS `none of these`)
       OR (`the matter` EQUALS `something else`)
       OR `I am a prisoner in custody`
       OR (NOT `a party asked the regulator to appoint an inspector`)
       OR (NOT `the dispute is still unresolved`)
       OR `the hours since that request` LESS THAN 24
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 102F(1): "A party to a dispute notified to SAET under this Division must bear the party's own costs in relation to the
-- dispute." (2): "However, SAET may order a party (the first party) to pay costs incurred by another party ... if SAET is
-- satisfied -- (a) the WHS matter the subject of the dispute is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in
-- substance; and (b) the first party notified the dispute to SAET or has otherwise acted without reasonable cause".
-- JUST TRUE: SAET may order me to pay. JUST FALSE: the "if" of (2) fails, so (1) leaves each party to its own costs.
GIVEN `SAET is satisfied the matter is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I notified the dispute or otherwise acted without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102F -- SAET may order me to pay another party's costs` `SAET is satisfied the matter is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance` `I notified the dispute or otherwise acted without reasonable cause` MEANS
    IF `SAET is satisfied the matter is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance` AND `I notified the dispute or otherwise acted without reasonable cause`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 6 Division 1 -- discriminatory, coercive and misleading conduct`

-- s 105(1), (2): the conduct (done, organised, or threatened).
DECLARE `What was done` IS ONE OF
    `I was dismissed`
    `my contract for services was terminated`
    `I was put to my detriment in my engagement`
    `my position was altered to my detriment`
    `I was refused or not offered engagement as a prospective worker`
    `I was offered less favourable terms than another prospective worker`
    `a commercial arrangement with me was terminated`
    `a commercial arrangement with me was refused or not entered into`
    `something else`

-- "a person engages in discriminatory conduct if": JUST FALSE for anything else.
GIVEN w IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 -- it is discriminatory conduct` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `something else` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 106 (a)-(j): the conduct is "engaged in for a prohibited reason if it is engaged in because" the person is, has been
-- or proposes to be, or does, has done or proposes to do, one of these things. (h) is raising an issue or concern about
-- work health and safety with one of the persons it lists (the business, an inspector, a WHS entry permit holder, a
-- health and safety representative, a committee member, another worker, any other duty holder, any other person
-- exercising a power or function under the Act).
DECLARE `Why it was done` IS ONE OF
    `my being a health and safety representative or committee member`
    `my undertaking another role under the Act`
    `my exercising powers or functions as a representative or committee member`
    `my exercising, or not exercising, a power under the Act`
    `my performing, or not performing, a function under the Act`
    `my assisting or giving information to a person exercising a power or function under the Act`
    `my raising a health and safety issue or concern with a person s 106(h) lists`
    `my raising a health and safety issue or concern with someone else`
    `my involvement in resolving a health and safety issue under the Act`
    `my taking action to seek compliance with a duty or obligation under the Act`
    `another reason`

GIVEN r IS A `Why it was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106 -- it is a prohibited reason` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `my raising a health and safety issue or concern with someone else` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `another reason` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ss 105 and 106 together: discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason (whether it was the dominant or a substantial
-- reason is for the court: ss 104(2), 110, 112(4), 113(2)).
GIVEN w IS A `What was done`, r IS A `Why it was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 105, 106 -- it is discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` w r MEANS
    IF (`s 105 -- it is discriminatory conduct` w EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 106 -- it is a prohibited reason` r EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 104(1) "must not engage in discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason"; (2): an offence "only if the reason ...
-- was the dominant reason". s 110: once the prosecution proves the conduct and the circumstance and it is alleged that it
-- was for a prohibited reason, the reason "is presumed to be the dominant reason ... unless the accused proves, on the
-- balance of probabilities, that the reason was not the dominant reason". JUST TRUE: an offence on these facts. JUST
-- FALSE: not discriminatory conduct, not a prohibited reason, or not the dominant reason. No evidence of the reason:
-- NOTHING-kind: the presumption is not engaged and dominance is for the court (fork F8).
GIVEN w IS A `What was done`
      r IS A `Why it was done`
      `there is evidence it was done for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proved that reason was not the dominant reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104 -- an offence of discriminatory conduct is made out` w r `there is evidence it was done for that reason` `the person proved that reason was not the dominant reason` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 105 -- it is discriminatory conduct` w EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT (`s 106 -- it is a prohibited reason` r EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the person proved that reason was not the dominant reason`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `there is evidence it was done for that reason`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING

-- s 108(1): "must not organise or take, or threaten to organise or take, any action against another person with intent to
-- coerce or induce the other person, or a third person" to exercise or not a power, perform or not a function, do so in a
-- particular way, or "refrain from seeking, or continuing to undertake, a role under this Act". (2): not taking an action
-- counts. (3): "a reasonable direction given by an emergency services worker in an emergency is not an action with intent
-- to coerce or induce a person" (s 4: police, the fire services, the State Emergency Service; reg 8A adds emergency
-- ambulance staff). JUST FALSE for (3); NOTHING-kind (a prohibition limited by its own wording) without the intent.
GIVEN `action was taken or threatened against me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was meant to coerce or induce me about a power, function or role under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was a reasonable direction of an emergency services worker in an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108 -- the person contravened the coercion prohibition` `action was taken or threatened against me` `it was meant to coerce or induce me about a power, function or role under the Act` `it was a reasonable direction of an emergency services worker in an emergency` MEANS
    IF `it was a reasonable direction of an emergency services worker in an emergency`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `action was taken or threatened against me` AND `it was meant to coerce or induce me about a power, function or role under the Act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- s 109(1): "must not knowingly or recklessly make a false or misleading representation to another person about that
-- other person's -- (a) rights or obligations under this Act; or (b) ability to initiate, or participate in, a process or
-- proceedings under this Act; or (c) ability to make a complaint or inquiry to a person or body empowered under this Act
-- to seek compliance with this Act." (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the person to whom the representation is made
-- would not be expected to rely on it." JUST FALSE for (2); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) otherwise.
GIVEN `it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made knowingly or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was about my rights, obligations, processes or complaints under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I would not be expected to rely on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109 -- the representation to me was prohibited` `it was false or misleading` `it was made knowingly or recklessly` `it was about my rights, obligations, processes or complaints under the Act` `I would not be expected to rely on it` MEANS
    IF `I would not be expected to rely on it`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it was false or misleading` AND `it was made knowingly or recklessly` AND `it was about my rights, obligations, processes or complaints under the Act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulative rules -- steps that must be taken in time`

-- "must be commenced not more than 1 year after" (s 113(1)); "within 48 hours of that requirement" (s 38(4)(b));
-- "Within 3 months after the regulator receives a request the regulator must -- (a) advise the person (in writing)"
-- (s 231(2)); "The application must be made ... within 14 days" or "28 days" (s 229(2)); "Proceedings under this section
-- must be instituted within 1 month after the day on which the contravention of the order first occurred" (s 260A(2)).
-- Each rule starts at 0 and allows a number of days (hours for s 38(4)(b)); FULFILLED means in time. They take DEONTIC
-- values, so they are never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `the business`
    `the regulator`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `commence the proceeding`
    `give the written notice of the incident`
    `advise the requester in writing`
    `apply to SAET for external review`
    `institute the proceeding for the contravened order`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 113(1) -- the proceeding must be commenced within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST `commence the proceeding`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 113(1): a proceeding under s 112 must be commenced not more than 1 year after the applicant knew or ought to have known that the cause of action accrued"

GIVEN `the hours allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 38(4)(b) -- the written notice must be given within` `the hours allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the business`
    MUST `give the written notice of the incident`
    WITHIN `the hours allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the business` BECAUSE "s 38(4)(b): the written notice of the incident was not given within 48 hours of the regulator's requirement"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 231(2) -- the regulator must advise within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the regulator`
    MUST `advise the requester in writing`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the regulator` BECAUSE "s 231(2): the regulator must advise the person in writing within 3 months after receiving the request"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 229(2) -- the application for external review must be made within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST `apply to SAET for external review`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 229(2): the application for external review must be made within 14 days (28 for a forfeiture) after the decision first came to the applicant's notice, or 14 days after a required statement of reasons"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 260A(2) -- the proceeding must be instituted within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST `institute the proceeding for the contravened order`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 260A(2): proceedings must be instituted within 1 month after the day on which the contravention of the order first occurred"

-- Whether a party taking a step at a time satisfies a rule.
GIVEN `the time of the step` IS A NUMBER, `the party` IS A `Party`, `the step` IS A `Step`, `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking the step at` `the time of the step` `by` `the party` `the step` `satisfies` `the rule` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the party` `the step` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether a step taken on a day is in time for a deadline that runs from a start day to a last day (both days counted).
-- A day before the start is in time.
GIVEN `the day of the step` IS A DATE, `the start day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE, `the party` IS A `Party`, `the step` IS A `Step`, `the rule maker` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a step on` `the day of the step` `is in time from` `the start day` `to` `the last day` `by` `the party` `the step` `under` `the rule maker` IF
    IF `the day of the step` `is before` `the start day`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `taking the step at` (`the days from` `the start day` `to` `the day of the step`) `by` `the party` `the step` `satisfies` (`the rule maker` (`the days from` `the start day` `to` `the last day`))

§§ `Part 6 Divisions 3 and 4 -- my civil proceeding in SAET`

-- s 112(2): the three kinds of conduct SAET may make orders about.
DECLARE `Kind of complaint` IS ONE OF
    `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason`
    `asking, instructing, inducing, encouraging, authorising or assisting another to engage in it`
    `coercion or inducement contrary to s 108`

-- s 113(1): "not more than 1 year after the date on which the applicant knew or ought to have known that the cause of
-- action accrued". "After the date" excludes the day: the last day is the first anniversary (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day I knew or ought to have known` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113(1) -- the last day to commence` `the day I knew or ought to have known` MEANS
    `the anniversary` 1 `years after` `the day I knew or ought to have known`

-- s 112(1), (6): "An eligible person may apply to SAET for an order under this section"; "each of the following is an
-- eligible person: (a) a person affected by the contravention; (b) a person authorised as a representative by a person
-- referred to in paragraph (a)." s 113(1): the 1 year. s 115: "A person cannot -- (a) commence a proceeding under Division
-- 3 ... if the person has commenced a proceeding or made an application or complaint in relation to the same matter under
-- a law of the Commonwealth or a State and that proceeding, application or complaint has not been withdrawn; ... (c)
-- commence or continue an application under Division 3 ... if the person has failed in a proceeding, application or
-- complaint in relation to the same matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a State, other than a proceeding,
-- application or complaint relating to workers' compensation." JUST FALSE for s 113(1) and s 115 ("must", "cannot");
-- not an eligible person: NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording (fork F9).
GIVEN `I am affected, or authorised by an affected person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I knew or ought to have known` IS A DATE
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE
      `I have another unwithdrawn proceeding on the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I failed in another proceeding on the same matter, not about workers compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112 -- I may apply to SAET` `I am affected, or authorised by an affected person` `the day I knew or ought to have known` `the day I apply` `I have another unwithdrawn proceeding on the same matter` `I failed in another proceeding on the same matter, not about workers compensation` MEANS
    IF `I have another unwithdrawn proceeding on the same matter` OR `I failed in another proceeding on the same matter, not about workers compensation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT (`a step on` `the day I apply` `is in time from` `the day I knew or ought to have known` `to` (`s 113(1) -- the last day to commence` `the day I knew or ought to have known`) `by` `the applicant` `commence the proceeding` `under` `s 113(1) -- the proceeding must be commenced within`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `I am affected, or authorised by an affected person`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING

-- SAET's findings in one civil proceeding, entered as facts.
DECLARE `Civil case` HAS
    `the complaint`                      IS A `Kind of complaint`
    `what was done`                      IS A `What was done`
    `why it was done`                    IS A `Why it was done`
    `the defendant proved the reason was not a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant proved the conduct was reasonable and mainly to comply with WHS law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `coercion contravention`             IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `a s 111 order was made for the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was compensated for the matter under another law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Whether SAET may find the conduct proved. For (2)(a) and (b): discriminatory conduct (s 105), a prohibited reason
-- (s 106), presumed a substantial reason (s 113(2)) "unless the defendant proves ... that the reason was not a substantial
-- reason", and "may be found ... only if a reason ... was a substantial reason" (s 112(4)); the s 113(3) defence ("the
-- conduct was reasonable in the circumstances; and a substantial reason for the conduct was to comply with the
-- requirements of this Act or a corresponding WHS law"); s 114(3): after a s 111 order "SAET cannot make an order under
-- section 112" for the same conduct. For (2)(c): the s 108 answer.
GIVEN c IS A `Civil case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 112-114 -- SAET may find the complaint proved` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the complaint`
    WHEN `coercion or inducement contrary to s 108` THEN c's `coercion contravention`
    OTHERWISE
        IF NOT (`s 105 -- it is discriminatory conduct` (c's `what was done`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF NOT (`s 106 -- it is a prohibited reason` (c's `why it was done`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE IF c's `the defendant proved the reason was not a substantial reason`
                       OR c's `the defendant proved the conduct was reasonable and mainly to comply with WHS law`
                       OR c's `a s 111 order was made for the same conduct`
                  THEN JUST FALSE
                  ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Order` IS ONE OF
    `an injunction`
    `compensation`
    `reinstatement, re-employment or employment`
    `any other order SAET considers appropriate`

-- s 112(3): "(a) an injunction; or (b) in the case of conduct referred to in subsection (2)(a) or (b), an order that the
-- person pay (within a specified period) the compensation ...; or (c) in the case of conduct referred to in subsection
-- (2)(a) in relation to a worker who was or is an employee or prospective employee, an order that -- (i) the worker be
-- reinstated or re-employed ...; or (ii) the prospective worker be employed ...; or (d) any other order that SAET
-- considers appropriate." s 115(b): a person cannot "recover any compensation under Division 3 ... if the person has
-- received compensation for the matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a State". The application must also be open
-- (`s 112 -- I may apply to SAET`). Compensation for (2)(c), or reinstatement outside (2)(a) or for a worker who was not
-- an employee: NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording; (d) may still reach it (fork F10).
GIVEN `may apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, c IS A `Civil case`, o IS AN `Order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(3) -- SAET may make the order for me` `may apply` c o MEANS
    IF NOT (`may apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN `may apply`
    ELSE IF NOT (`ss 112-114 -- SAET may find the complaint proved` c EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN `ss 112-114 -- SAET may find the complaint proved` c
         ELSE CONSIDER o
              WHEN `compensation` THEN
                  IF c's `the complaint` EQUALS `coercion or inducement contrary to s 108`
                  THEN NOTHING
                  ELSE IF c's `I was compensated for the matter under another law`
                       THEN JUST FALSE
                       ELSE JUST TRUE
              WHEN `reinstatement, re-employment or employment` THEN
                  IF (c's `the complaint` EQUALS `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason`) AND c's `I was or am an employee or prospective employee`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 111: "If a person is convicted or found guilty of an offence under section 104 or 107, the court may (in addition to
-- imposing a penalty) make either or both of the following orders: (a) ... compensation to the person who was the subject
-- of the discriminatory conduct ...; (b) in relation to a person who was or is an employee or prospective employee, an
-- order that" the person be reinstated, re-employed or employed. s 114(2): after an order by SAET under s 112 for the same
-- conduct "the court cannot make an order under section 111". No conviction: NOTHING-kind: the "if" of a power unmet
-- (fork F7).
GIVEN `the person was convicted or found guilty under s 104 or 107` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 112 order was made for the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      o IS AN `Order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111 -- the criminal court may make the order for me` `the person was convicted or found guilty under s 104 or 107` `a s 112 order was made for the same conduct` `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` o MEANS
    IF `a s 112 order was made for the same conduct`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `the person was convicted or found guilty under s 104 or 107`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE CONSIDER o
              WHEN `compensation` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `reinstatement, re-employment or employment` THEN
                  IF `I was or am an employee or prospective employee`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING
              OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 260A -- proceedings for a contravened SAET arbitration order`

-- s 260A(1): "If an order made for the purposes of arbitration under section 102C(3) or 142(3) is contravened,
-- proceedings may be brought in SAET against a person for the contravention of the relevant WHS civil penalty provision by
-- a person affected by the contravention of the order." (2): "must be instituted within 1 month after the day on which
-- the contravention of the order first occurred." Not a SAET arbitration order, not contravened, or out of time: JUST
-- FALSE ("if", a period the Act fixes); not affected: NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording.
GIVEN `the day the contravention first occurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 260A(2) -- the last day to institute` `the day the contravention first occurred` MEANS
    `the date` 1 `months after` `the day the contravention first occurred`

GIVEN `it is a SAET arbitration order under s 102C(3) or 142(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was contravened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am affected by the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the contravention first occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day I institute` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 260A -- I may bring proceedings for the contravened order` `it is a SAET arbitration order under s 102C(3) or 142(3)` `the order was contravened` `I am affected by the contravention` `the day the contravention first occurred` `the day I institute` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a SAET arbitration order under s 102C(3) or 142(3)`) OR (NOT `the order was contravened`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT (`a step on` `the day I institute` `is in time from` `the day the contravention first occurred` `to` (`s 260A(2) -- the last day to institute` `the day the contravention first occurred`) `by` `the applicant` `institute the proceeding for the contravened order` `under` `s 260A(2) -- the proceeding must be instituted within`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `I am affected by the contravention`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING

-- s 260A(4): "If, in proceedings under this section, SAET finds that a party has contravened an order ..., SAET should (in
-- addition to any monetary penalty imposed) also order that the contravening party pay the applicant's reasonable costs
-- in relation to the proceedings unless SAET is satisfied that it would be contrary to the interests of justice to make
-- such an order." JUST FALSE where SAET does not find the contravention ("if") or is satisfied of the exception
-- ("unless").
GIVEN `SAET finds the order was contravened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `SAET is satisfied a costs order would be contrary to the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 260A(4) -- SAET should order my reasonable costs` `SAET finds the order was contravened` `SAET is satisfied a costs order would be contrary to the interests of justice` MEANS
    IF `SAET finds the order was contravened` AND (NOT `SAET is satisfied a costs order would be contrary to the interests of justice`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Fines and civil penalties for contraventions that touch me`

DECLARE `Offender` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body corporate`

DECLARE `Contravention` IS ONE OF
    `not notifying the regulator of a notifiable incident (s 38(1))`
    `not keeping the record of a notifiable incident (s 38(7))`
    `disturbing an incident site (s 39(1))`
    `contravening a SAET arbitration order in a WHS dispute (s 102C(4))`
    `discriminatory conduct (s 104)`
    `requesting, inducing or assisting discriminatory conduct (s 107)`
    `coercion or inducement (s 108)`
    `misrepresentation about my rights (s 109)`
    `levying or charging me for work health and safety (s 273)`

-- The maximum, in dollars ("Maximum penalty" under each section; for s 102C(4) a WHS civil penalty).
GIVEN k IS A `Contravention`, p IS AN `Offender`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum penalty for the contravention` k `by` p MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `not notifying the regulator of a notifiable incident (s 38(1))` THEN `individual or body` 10000 50000
    WHEN `not keeping the record of a notifiable incident (s 38(7))` THEN `individual or body` 5000 25000
    WHEN `disturbing an incident site (s 39(1))` THEN `individual or body` 10000 50000
    WHEN `contravening a SAET arbitration order in a WHS dispute (s 102C(4))` THEN `individual or body` 10000 100000
    WHEN `levying or charging me for work health and safety (s 273)` THEN `individual or body` 5000 25000
    OTHERWISE `individual or body` 100000 500000
    WHERE
        `individual or body` i b MEANS
            CONSIDER p
            WHEN `an individual` THEN i
            OTHERWISE b

§§ `s 184 -- compensation for an inspector's entry powers`

-- s 184(1): "A person may claim compensation from the State if the person incurs loss or expense because of the exercise
-- or purported exercise of a power under Division 3 of this Part" (powers relating to entry: entry, search warrants,
-- production of documents and answers, copying, seizure, ss 163-183). (3): "The court may order compensation to be paid
-- only if it is satisfied it is just to make the order in the circumstances of the particular case." JUST FALSE where
-- the loss did not come from a Division 3 power ("if") or the court is not satisfied it is just ("only if").
GIVEN `I incurred loss or expense because of an inspector's entry, search, seizure or document power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied it is just to order compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184 -- the court may order the State to compensate me` `I incurred loss or expense because of an inspector's entry, search, seizure or document power` `the court is satisfied it is just to order compensation` MEANS
    IF `I incurred loss or expense because of an inspector's entry, search, seizure or document power` AND `the court is satisfied it is just to order compensation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 12 -- review of decisions`

-- s 223(1): the table of reviewable decisions and, for each, "who is eligible to apply for review". (1a): a worker
-- includes the worker's representative.
DECLARE `Reviewable decision` IS ONE OF
    `a decision after a failure to commence work group negotiations (s 54(2))`
    `a decision about training of a health and safety representative (s 72(7))`
    `a decision about a health and safety committee (s 76(6))`
    `an inspector's decision on review of a provisional improvement notice (s 102)`
    `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179)`
    `a decision about return of seized things (s 180)`
    `the issue of an improvement notice (s 191)`
    `an extension of time to comply with an improvement notice (s 194)`
    `the issue of a prohibition notice (s 195)`
    `the issue of a non-disturbance notice (s 198)`
    `the issue of a subsequent notice (s 201)`
    `the regulator's variation or cancellation of a notice (s 207)`
    `a decision under a prescribed provision of the regulations`

-- The eligible persons the table names that a worker can be: "A worker whose interests are affected by the decision"
-- (items 1, 3, 4, 7-12); "The person to whom the ... notice was issued" (items 4, 7-12); "The person entitled to the
-- thing" (items 5, 6). Item 2 names no worker. The table closes the list ("who is eligible"): JUST FALSE where the person
-- is not named. Item 13: the regulations name the eligible persons (reg 676, licensing and similar decisions, not
-- encoded): NOTHING-kind: points outside the encoded provisions.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Reviewable decision`
      `my interests as a worker are affected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was issued to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the person entitled to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223 -- I am an eligible person` `the decision` `my interests as a worker are affected` `the notice was issued to me` `I am the person entitled to the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a decision under a prescribed provision of the regulations` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a decision about training of a health and safety representative (s 72(7))` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179)` THEN `yes or no` `I am the person entitled to the thing`
    WHEN `a decision about return of seized things (s 180)` THEN `yes or no` `I am the person entitled to the thing`
    WHEN `a decision after a failure to commence work group negotiations (s 54(2))` THEN `yes or no` `my interests as a worker are affected`
    WHEN `a decision about a health and safety committee (s 76(6))` THEN `yes or no` `my interests as a worker are affected`
    OTHERWISE `yes or no` (`my interests as a worker are affected` OR `the notice was issued to me`)
    WHERE
        `yes or no` b MEANS
            IF b
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 224(1): "An eligible person in relation to a reviewable decision, other than a decision made by the regulator or a
-- delegate of the regulator, may apply to the regulator for review (an internal review) of the decision within -- (a) the
-- prescribed time after the day on which the decision first came to the eligible person's notice; or (b) such longer
-- period as the regulator allows." (3): the prescribed time is "(a) in the case of a decision to issue an improvement
-- notice the period specified in the notice for compliance with the notice or 14 days, whichever is the lesser; and (b)
-- in any other case, 14 days." The day of notice excluded (fork F1). A decision of the regulator or its delegate: NOTHING
-- (no internal review; external review lies, s 229(1)(a)).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Reviewable decision`
      `the regulator or its delegate made it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it came to my notice` IS A DATE
      `the days the notice allows for compliance` IS A NUMBER
      `the further days the regulator allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 224 -- the last day to apply for internal review` `the decision` `the regulator or its delegate made it` `the day it came to my notice` `the days the notice allows for compliance` `the further days the regulator allowed` MEANS
    IF `the regulator or its delegate made it`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the day` (`the prescribed time` PLUS `the further days the regulator allowed`) `days after` `the day it came to my notice`)
    WHERE
        `the prescribed time` MEANS
            IF `the decision` EQUALS `the issue of an improvement notice (s 191)`
            THEN min `the days the notice allows for compliance` 14
            ELSE 14

-- s 226(1): "The internal reviewer must ... make a decision ... within 14 days after the application for internal review
-- is received." (3): "If the internal reviewer seeks further information from the applicant, the 14 day period ceases to
-- run until the applicant provides the information". (6): "If the reviewable decision is not varied or set aside within
-- the 14 day period, the decision is taken to have been confirmed by the internal reviewer." The last day of the period
-- (counting the days it stopped); if nothing is decided by then, the decision stands confirmed.
GIVEN `the day the application was received` IS A DATE, `the days the period stopped for information` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 226 -- the last day of the internal review` `the day the application was received` `the days the period stopped for information` MEANS
    `the day` (14 PLUS `the days the period stopped for information`) `days after` `the day the application was received`

-- s 228(1): "An application for an internal review of a reviewable decision (other than a decision to issue a prohibition
-- notice or a non-disturbance notice) stays the operation of the decision." (2): for those two, "the reviewer may stay the
-- operation of the decision"; (4), (5): a decision on an application for a stay is due within 1 working day, failing which
-- "the reviewer is taken to have made a decision to grant a stay". JUST TRUE: stayed. JUST FALSE: a prohibition or
-- non-disturbance notice that the reviewer has not stayed (no application, or refused in time).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Reviewable decision`
      `a stay was applied for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reviewer decided the stay application within 1 working day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reviewer granted a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228 -- the decision is stayed pending internal review` `the decision` `a stay was applied for` `the reviewer decided the stay application within 1 working day` `the reviewer granted a stay` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the decision` EQUALS `the issue of a prohibition notice (s 195)`)) AND (NOT (`the decision` EQUALS `the issue of a non-disturbance notice (s 198)`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the reviewer granted a stay`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `a stay was applied for` AND (NOT `the reviewer decided the stay application within 1 working day`)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 229(2): "The application must be made -- (a) if the decision was to forfeit a thing ..., within 28 days after the day
-- on which the decision first came to the applicant's notice; or (b) in the case of any other decision, within 14 days
-- after the day on which the decision first came to the applicant's notice; or (c) if the regulator is required by the
-- external review body to give the eligible person a statement of reasons, within 14 days after the day on which the
-- statement is provided." Read: (c) gives a further period where it applies; the last day is the later (fork F14).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Reviewable decision`
      `the day it came to my notice` IS A DATE
      `I was given a statement of reasons SAET required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the statement was provided` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 229(2) -- the last day to apply for external review` `the decision` `the day it came to my notice` `I was given a statement of reasons SAET required` `the day the statement was provided` MEANS
    IF `I was given a statement of reasons SAET required`
    THEN `the later of` `the (a) or (b) day` `and` (`the day` 14 `days after` `the day the statement was provided`)
    ELSE `the (a) or (b) day`
    WHERE
        `the (a) or (b) day` MEANS
            IF `the decision` EQUALS `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179)`
            THEN `the day` 28 `days after` `the day it came to my notice`
            ELSE `the day` 14 `days after` `the day it came to my notice`

-- s 229(1): "An eligible person may apply to SAET ... for a review of -- (a) a reviewable decision made by the regulator; or
-- (b) a decision made, or taken to have been made, on an internal review." Not one of those two: JUST FALSE (the decision
-- must first go to internal review, s 224); not eligible: the s 223 answer; late: JUST FALSE (a period the Act fixes).
GIVEN `eligible` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is the regulator's decision or an internal review decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day` IS A DATE
      `the day it came to my notice` IS A DATE
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 229 -- I may apply to SAET for external review` `eligible` `it is the regulator's decision or an internal review decision` `the last day` `the day it came to my notice` `the day I apply` MEANS
    IF NOT (`eligible` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN `eligible`
    ELSE IF NOT `it is the regulator's decision or an internal review decision`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `a step on` `the day I apply` `is in time from` `the day it came to my notice` `to` `the last day` `by` `the applicant` `apply to SAET for external review` `under` `s 229(2) -- the application for external review must be made within`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 230-232 -- prosecution`

DECLARE `Offence I consider was committed` IS ONE OF
    `industrial manslaughter`
    `a Category 1 offence`
    `a Category 2 offence`
    `a Category 3 offence or another offence against the Act`

DECLARE `Ground for my view` IS ONE OF
    `what happened itself (s 231(1)(a)(i))`
    `a coronial report or inquest (s 231(1)(a)(ii))`

-- s 231(1): "This section applies if -- (a) a person -- (i) reasonably considers that the occurrence of an act, matter or
-- thing constitutes an industrial manslaughter offence, a Category 1 offence or a Category 2 offence; or (ii) reasonably
-- considers, from a coronial report or the proceedings at a coronial inquiry or inquest, that [such an offence] has been
-- committed; and (b) no prosecution for the offence has been brought." (1a): "The person may make a written request to the
-- regulator that a prosecution be brought." (1b): "The request may only be made -- (a) if subsection (1)(a)(i) applies --
-- at least 6 months, but no more than 24 months after the act, matter or thing occurs; or (b) if subsection (1)(a)(ii)
-- applies -- within 12 months after the report is made or the inquiry or inquest ends." Read: from the day 6 months after
-- the occurrence to the day 24 months after, both included; from the day of the report to the day 12 months after
-- (fork F2). Outside the window, a Category 3 offence, or a prosecution already brought: JUST FALSE ("applies if", "may
-- only"). s 230(1): the prosecution itself "may only be brought by" the regulator or an authorised inspector (and the
-- Director of Public Prosecutions, s 230(9)), not by the person.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence I consider was committed`
      `the ground` IS A `Ground for my view`
      `I reasonably consider it was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a prosecution has been brought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it occurred, or of the report or end of the inquest` IS A DATE
      `the day of my request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(1) -- I may request a prosecution` `the offence` `the ground` `I reasonably consider it was committed` `a prosecution has been brought` `the day it occurred, or of the report or end of the inquest` `the day of my request` MEANS
    IF `the offence` EQUALS `a Category 3 offence or another offence against the Act`
       OR (NOT `I reasonably consider it was committed`)
       OR `a prosecution has been brought`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (NOT (`the day of my request` `is before` `the first day`))
            AND (NOT (`the day of my request` `is after` `the last day`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the first day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the ground`
            WHEN `what happened itself (s 231(1)(a)(i))` THEN `the date` 6 `months after` `the day it occurred, or of the report or end of the inquest`
            OTHERWISE `the day it occurred, or of the report or end of the inquest`
        `the last day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the ground`
            WHEN `what happened itself (s 231(1)(a)(i))` THEN `the date` 24 `months after` `the day it occurred, or of the report or end of the inquest`
            OTHERWISE `the date` 12 `months after` `the day it occurred, or of the report or end of the inquest`

-- s 231(2): "Within 3 months after the regulator receives a request": the last day is the same day 3 months later (F1).
GIVEN `the day the regulator received it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 231(2) -- the last day for the regulator's advice` `the day the regulator received it` MEANS
    `the date` 3 `months after` `the day the regulator received it`

-- s 231(2): whether the regulator's written advice came within 3 months after it received the request. JUST TRUE: in
-- time. JUST FALSE: late, or not yet given and the last day has passed. Not yet given and still within time: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the day the regulator received my request` IS A DATE
      `the regulator has advised me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the advice, or today if none` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(2) -- the regulator advised me in time` `the day the regulator received my request` `the regulator has advised me` `the day of the advice, or today if none` MEANS
    IF `the regulator has advised me`
    THEN IF `a step on` `the day of the advice, or today if none` `is in time from` `the day the regulator received my request` `to` (`s 231(2) -- the last day for the regulator's advice` `the day the regulator received my request`) `by` `the regulator` `advise the requester in writing` `under` `s 231(2) -- the regulator must advise within`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the day of the advice, or today if none` `is after` (`s 231(2) -- the last day for the regulator's advice` `the day the regulator received my request`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- s 231(2a): "If ... the regulator advises the person that the investigation is not complete, the regulator must -- (a)
-- until the investigation is complete, give the person a written update about the investigation at least every 3
-- months". The next update is due by the day 3 months after the last advice or update (F1). Investigation complete:
-- NOTHING (no further update is due; a notice of the outcome is due under (2a)(b), with no time stated).
GIVEN `the investigation is complete` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of the last advice or update` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 231(2a) -- the last day for my next update` `the investigation is complete` `the day of the last advice or update` MEANS
    IF `the investigation is complete`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the date` 3 `months after` `the day of the last advice or update`)

-- s 231(3): "If the regulator advises the person under subsection (2) or (2a) that a prosecution for an industrial
-- manslaughter, Category 1 or Category 2 offence will not be brought, the regulator must -- (a) advise the person that
-- the person may ask the regulator to refer the matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions for consideration; and (b)
-- if the person makes a written request to the regulator to do so, refer the matter to the Director of Public
-- Prosecutions within 1 month of the request." No such advice, or a Category 3 offence: NOTHING (no referral is due).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence I consider was committed`
      `the regulator advised that no prosecution will be brought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I asked in writing for a referral` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 231(3)(b) -- the last day to refer my matter to the DPP` `the offence` `the regulator advised that no prosecution will be brought` `the day I asked in writing for a referral` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the regulator advised that no prosecution will be brought`) OR (`the offence` EQUALS `a Category 3 offence or another offence against the Act`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the date` 1 `months after` `the day I asked in writing for a referral`)

-- s 231(4): "The Director of Public Prosecutions must consider the matter and advise (in writing) the regulator within 1
-- month as to whether the Director considers that a prosecution should be brought." The month is read from the referral
-- (finding 2; fork F15).
GIVEN `the day the matter was referred to the DPP` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 231(4) -- the last day for the DPP's advice` `the day the matter was referred to the DPP` MEANS
    `the date` 1 `months after` `the day the matter was referred to the DPP`

DECLARE `Prosecution time` IS ONE OF
    `no limitation period applies`
    `the last day to bring the prosecution is` HAS `the final day` IS A DATE

-- s 232(1): "Proceedings for an offence against this Act may be brought within the latest of the following periods to
-- occur: (a) within 2 years after the offence first comes to the notice of the regulator; (b) within 1 year after a
-- coronial report was made or a coronial inquiry or inquest ended, if it appeared from the report or the proceedings at
-- the inquiry or inquest that an offence had been committed against this Act; (ba) if a matter has been referred to the
-- Director of Public Prosecutions under section 231(3)(b), within 1 month after the Director provides the regulator with
-- advice under section 231(4) ...; (c) if a WHS undertaking has been given in relation to the offence, within 6 months
-- after -- (i) the WHS undertaking is contravened; or (ii) it comes to the notice of the regulator that the WHS
-- undertaking has been contravened; or (iii) the regulator has agreed under section 221 to the withdrawal of the WHS
-- undertaking." (2): a Category 1 offence may be brought later "if fresh evidence relevant to the offence is discovered
-- and the court is satisfied that the evidence could not reasonably have been discovered within the relevant limitation
-- period". (3): "This section does not apply to proceedings for an industrial manslaughter offence." "Within 2 years
-- after" a day excludes the day: the last day is the anniversary (fork F1); the (c) triggers entered as their latest day
-- (fork F11).
DECLARE `Prosecution facts` HAS
    `the offence charged`                         IS AN `Offence I consider was committed`
    `the day it came to the regulator's notice`   IS A DATE
    `a coronial report or inquest showed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the report was made or the inquest ended` IS A DATE
    `the matter was referred to the DPP`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the DPP advised the regulator`       IS A DATE
    `a WHS undertaking was given and later breached or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the latest day of breach, its notice or withdrawal` IS A DATE
    `fresh evidence the court accepts for a Category 1 offence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS A `Prosecution facts`
GIVETH A `Prosecution time`
`s 232 -- the time for prosecution` f MEANS
    IF f's `the offence charged` EQUALS `industrial manslaughter`
    THEN `no limitation period applies`
    ELSE IF (f's `the offence charged` EQUALS `a Category 1 offence`) AND f's `fresh evidence the court accepts for a Category 1 offence`
         THEN `no limitation period applies`
         ELSE `the last day to bring the prosecution is` (`the later of` `the (a) day` `and` (`the later of` `the (b) day` `and` (`the later of` `the (ba) day` `and` `the (c) day`)))
    WHERE
        `the (a) day` MEANS `the anniversary` 2 `years after` (f's `the day it came to the regulator's notice`)
        `the (b) day` MEANS
            IF f's `a coronial report or inquest showed an offence`
            THEN `the anniversary` 1 `years after` (f's `the day the report was made or the inquest ended`)
            ELSE `the (a) day`
        `the (ba) day` MEANS
            IF f's `the matter was referred to the DPP`
            THEN `the date` 1 `months after` (f's `the day the DPP advised the regulator`)
            ELSE `the (a) day`
        `the (c) day` MEANS
            IF f's `a WHS undertaking was given and later breached or withdrawn`
            THEN `the date` 6 `months after` (f's `the latest day of breach, its notice or withdrawal`)
            ELSE `the (a) day`

-- Whether a prosecution brought on a day is in time: JUST TRUE with no limitation period or on or before the last day;
-- JUST FALSE after it.
GIVEN t IS A `Prosecution time`, `the day of prosecution` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232 -- a prosecution on the day is in time` t `the day of prosecution` MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `no limitation period applies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the last day to bring the prosecution is` `the last` THEN
        IF `the day of prosecution` `is after` `the last`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 267, 272, 273 -- my rights against the business`

DECLARE `Provision contravened` IS ONE OF
    `discriminatory or coercive conduct (ss 104, 107, 108)`
    `misrepresentation (s 109)`
    `a SAET arbitration order in a WHS dispute or entry dispute (ss 102C(3), 142(3))`
    `another WHS civil penalty provision`
    `any other provision, such as a health and safety duty in Part 2`

-- s 267: "Except as provided in Part 6 and Part 7 and Division 7 of this Part, nothing in this Act is to be construed as
-- -- (a) conferring a right of action in civil proceedings in relation to a contravention of a provision of this Act; or
-- (b) conferring a defence to an action in civil proceedings or otherwise affecting a right of action in civil
-- proceedings". s 112 gives the person affected a proceeding for ss 104, 107 and 108; s 260A (in Division 7) gives a
-- person affected a proceeding for a contravened arbitration order. s 260: other WHS civil penalty proceedings "may only
-- be brought by -- (a) the regulator; or (b) an inspector". s 109 is in Part 6 but s 112 does not reach it (finding 3):
-- NOTHING-kind: the text is silent. Any other provision: JUST FALSE (the flat negative of s 267(a)).
GIVEN p IS A `Provision contravened`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267 -- the Act gives me a civil right of action` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `discriminatory or coercive conduct (ss 104, 107, 108)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a SAET arbitration order in a WHS dispute or entry dispute (ss 102C(3), 142(3))` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `misrepresentation (s 109)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 272: "A term of any agreement or contract that purports to exclude, limit or modify the operation of this Act or any
-- duty owed under this Act or to transfer to another person any duty owed under this Act is void." Any other term:
-- NOTHING-kind: the section is silent.
GIVEN `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term transfers a duty under the Act to someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272 -- the term is void` `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it` `the term transfers a duty under the Act to someone else` MEANS
    IF `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it` OR `the term transfers a duty under the Act to someone else`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 273: "A person conducting a business or undertaking must not impose a levy or charge on a worker, or permit a levy or
-- charge to be imposed on a worker, for anything done, or provided, in relation to work health and safety." JUST FALSE:
-- the business may not charge me. Another charge: NOTHING-kind: the section is silent.
GIVEN `I am a worker of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is for something done or provided for work health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 273 -- the business may charge me` `I am a worker of the business` `the charge is for something done or provided for work health and safety` MEANS
    IF `I am a worker of the business` AND `the charge is for something done or provided for work health and safety`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 38(4)(b) -- was the written notice given in time`

-- s 38(4)(b): a person who notified by telephone must "if required by the regulator, give a written notice of the
-- incident within 48 hours of that requirement being made". Counted in hours from the requirement. JUST TRUE: given in
-- time. JUST FALSE: given late, or not given and the 48 hours have passed. Not required: NOTHING-kind: the duty does not
-- arise (fork F7). Not given and the 48 hours have not passed: NOTHING (still open).
GIVEN `the regulator required a written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the written notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours after the requirement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(4)(b) -- the written notice was given in time` `the regulator required a written notice` `the written notice was given` `the hours after the requirement` MEANS
    IF NOT `the regulator required a written notice`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the written notice was given`
         THEN IF `taking the step at` `the hours after the requirement` `by` `the business` `give the written notice of the incident` `satisfies` (`s 38(4)(b) -- the written notice must be given within` 48)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the hours after the requirement` GREATER THAN 48
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE NOTHING
